# Chapter 14: Production Improvements

> *Scaling a Microsoft Sentinel proof of concept into an enterprise-ready Security Operations Center.*

---

# Overview

Building a successful Microsoft Sentinel lab demonstrates an understanding of cloud-native security operations. However, enterprise Security Operations Centers (SOCs) require additional considerations beyond basic deployment and detection engineering.

Production environments must address scalability, reliability, governance, automation, cost management, compliance, and continuous improvement. Detection logic must evolve as attackers change their techniques, while operational processes must ensure consistent monitoring across diverse environments.

This chapter explores how the Microsoft Sentinel implementation developed in this project could be expanded into a production-ready deployment capable of supporting enterprise security operations.

---

# From Lab to Production

The lab implementation focused on:

- Creating an Azure Resource Group.
- Deploying Azure Log Analytics Workspace.
- Enabling Microsoft Sentinel.
- Importing custom authentication logs.
- Writing KQL queries.
- Building Analytics Rules.
- Investigating SSH brute-force activity.
- Mapping detections to MITRE ATT&CK.

A production deployment extends these capabilities across an organization's entire infrastructure.

