# Cost Optimization

Microsoft Sentinel deployments should balance visibility with operational cost.

Best practices include:

- Ingest only required telemetry.
- Configure appropriate retention policies.
- Filter unnecessary logs before ingestion.
- Monitor daily data ingestion.
- Archive older logs when appropriate.
- Regularly review workspace usage.

Effective cost management ensures long-term sustainability without sacrificing security visibility.

---

# Access Control and Governance

Operational security is essential for protecting the SIEM itself.

Recommended practices include:

- Implement Role-Based Access Control (RBAC).
- Apply the principle of least privilege.
- Enable multi-factor authentication for administrators.
- Audit administrative actions.
- Review access permissions regularly.
- Protect API keys and shared secrets.

Governance reduces the risk of unauthorized access and configuration changes.

---

# Operational Metrics

SOC maturity should be measured using objective metrics.

Common Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) include:

| Metric | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| Mean Time to Detect (MTTD) | Time required to identify an incident |
| Mean Time to Respond (MTTR) | Time required to contain and remediate an incident |
| Alert Volume | Total alerts generated over time |
| False Positive Rate | Percentage of non-malicious alerts |
| Detection Coverage | ATT&CK techniques monitored |
| Automation Rate | Percentage of incidents handled through automation |

Monitoring these metrics supports continuous improvement.

